# ReadyNow Twilio Service - environment template.
#
# Copy to twilio/.env and fill in. The Serverless Toolkit uploads every
# variable in .env on deploy. twilio/.env is gitignored and must stay that
# way: it carries live database credentials and API keys.
#
# NOT set here, on purpose:
#   ACCOUNT_SID / AUTH_TOKEN  - supplied by the Service setting "Add my Twilio
#                               Credentials (ACCOUNT_SID) and (AUTH_TOKEN) to
#                               ENV". It is OFF by default. alert.js and
#                               alert-status.js both fail without it, and
#                               alert-status.js fails by rejecting every
#                               genuine callback with a 403.
#   DOMAIN_NAME               - injected by the runtime.
#
# Limits: 450 bytes per variable, ~3 kB total once JSON encoded. DO_MYSQL_CA_CERT
# is the one at risk - verify it is not truncated after deploy.
#
# TWO FILES, NOT ONE. Copy this template twice:
#
#   .env.prod     -> production environment   (readynow-XXXX.twil.io)
#   .env.nonprod  -> non-production environment (readynow-XXXX-dev.twil.io)
#
# Differs between them:
#   DO_MYSQL_DATABASE          readynow_notifications  vs  readynow-nonprod
#   ALERT_STATUS_CALLBACK_URL  each environment's own domain
#   ALERT_SWEEP_SECRET         prod secret  vs  NONPROD_ALERT_SWEEP_SECRET
#   NILRA_API_URL / _API_KEY   production NILRA  vs  staging NILRA
#
# Same in both:
#   DO_MYSQL_HOST/USER/PASSWORD/PORT/CA_CERT  one cluster, two schemas
#   MONGODB_URI, NILRA_COUNTRIES_URL          shared on purpose (see db/README.md)
#
# Shared with production DELIBERATELY - do not "fix" these:
#   MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID   Non-production uses the production Messaging
#                           Service, so TestFlight builds send real SMS to real
#                           phones. That is the point: an alert that Twilio
#                           accepted is not an alert that arrived, and the only
#                           way to know delivery works is to watch a message
#                           land on a handset. Test with your own numbers.
#   EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN       Same reasoning for push.
#
# Still worth separating if you get the chance:
#   AUTH0_DOMAIN            is there a production tenant separate from
#                           hrf-alt-dev.us.auth0.com?
#   TWILIO_API_SECRET       distinct values mean a leaked non-prod key cannot
#   TWILIO_DISPATCH_SECRET  drive production

# --- Messaging -------------------------------------------------------------
MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=

# --- Alert delivery (/alert, /alert-status) --------------------------------
# Must point at THIS Service's own /alert-status, not the Classic one.
ALERT_STATUS_CALLBACK_URL=
ALERT_SWEEP_SECRET=
AUTH0_DOMAIN=

# --- DigitalOcean MySQL (/alert, /alert-status, /notification-manager) -----
DO_MYSQL_HOST=
DO_MYSQL_USER=
DO_MYSQL_PASSWORD=
DO_MYSQL_DATABASE=
DO_MYSQL_PORT=
DO_MYSQL_CA_CERT=

# --- NILRA (/nilra-api, /nilra-api-staging, /countries) --------------------
NILRA_API_URL=
NILRA_API_KEY=
NILRA_COUNTRIES_URL=
NILRA_API_URL_STAGING=
NILRA_API_KEY_STAGING=

# --- Client-facing secrets -------------------------------------------------
# TWILIO_API_SECRET ships inlined in the app bundle. It marks a request as
# coming from a ReadyNow build; it is not authentication.
TWILIO_API_SECRET=
# Server-side only. Never ship to a client - it authorises broadcast dispatch.
TWILIO_DISPATCH_SECRET=
EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- Feedback (/save) ------------------------------------------------------
MONGODB_URI=
# Set to "true" to reject unmarked feedback. Leave unset until old installs drain.
FEEDBACK_REQUIRE_KEY=

# --- Development only ------------------------------------------------------
# Only to run the web build against this Service in a browser. Leave unset in
# production: native builds do not enforce CORS.
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=
